      "math_academy_id": "e-8139",
      "problem": "What ratio describes the number of rhombuses to the number of triangles?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133630/assets/49a799c1ec4b9e7caadd4af8714aa1133f33e7012b76083e9b241d05b0d2fee7.png)",
      "worked_solution": "First, we count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $2$ rhombuses.\n\nThen, we count the number of triangles. We see that there are $3$ triangles.\n\nSo the ratio of rhombuses to triangles is $\\dfrac{2}{3}.$",
